the three numbers following the letter ‘f’ are the vertex
numbers that make up each facet. 

This version of the shape model has been shifted to eliminate
any COM-COF offset. It has also been migrated from PCK10 to PCK11.
In addition, the maplets were iterated a total of ten times,
which improved the quality of the topography.

MISSION = Multiple      \Name of mission
TARGET  = PHOBOS        \Target object
ORIGIN  = Ernst et al. 2023 https://doi.org/10.1186/s40623-023-01814-7
DATASRC = SPC           \ Shape model data source
SRCMOD  =phobos_g_148m_spc_obj_0000n00000_v004.obj \ Source OBJ
DENSITY = 1847.0 /[kg/m^3] bulk density
ROTATION = 2.28033E-4 /[rad/s] rotation rate of asteroid
POTENTIAL = -93.2190607637768 /[J/kg] reference potential
MASS = 6.4171E23 /[kg] mass of nearby body
XPOS = 9378. /[km] X coordinate of nearby mass
YPOS = 0. /[km] Y coordinate of nearby mass
ZPOS = 0. /[km] Z coordinate of nearby mass
